    "font size" : 9.564,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "ABSTRACT"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 8,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 107.52, 368.268, 504.558, 453.615 ],
    "font" : "NimbusRomNo9L-Regu",
    "font size" : 9.963,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "The main objective of this work is to show, through counterexamples, that some of the theorems presented in the papers of Sharma et al. (2018) and Chauhan et al. ( 2021) are incorrect. Although they used these theorems to establish a sufﬁcient condition for a multi-twisted (MT) code to be linear complementary dual (LCD), we show that this condition itself remains valid. We further improve this condition by removing the restrictions on the shift constants and relaxing the required coprimality condition. We show that compared to the previous condition, the modiﬁed condition is able to identify more LCD MT codes. Furthermore, without the need for a normalized set of generators, we develop a formula to determine the dimension of any ρ-generator MT code."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 9,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 71.641, 327.948, 484.384, 354.032 ],
    "font" : "NimbusRomNo9L-Regu",
    "font size" : 9.963,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "Keywords Multi-twisted code · linear complementary dual · Determinantal divisors · Algebraic coding MSC: 94B05, 94B60, 11T71"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 10,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 72.002, 297.658, 154.609, 308.644 ],
    "font" : "NimbusRomNo9L-Medi",
